Only potential causes for the "double metric count":

- Exporter running twice

- Cloudflare API returning overlapping results

- Prometheus scraping multiple times

- Different zone lists, accounts, or time windows

_____________________________________________________________






Exporter querying Cloudflare API twice per scrape

Example Scenario:
Prometheus scrapes every 30s

Exporter is misconfigured to trigger two GraphQL calls per scrape
Result: You get roughly double count in the metrics → rate() also doubles


Inside exporter logs, look for duplicate GraphQL logs for same zone/time:
INFO[2025-07-24 21:24:05] Successfully HTTPRequestsEdgeCountryMetrics totalsmap[zone_count:4] 
INFO[2025-07-24 21:24:05] Successfully HTTPRequestsEdgeCountryMetrics totalsmap[zone_count:4] 



Exporter being scraped twice (duplicate targets in Prometheus)

- job_name: cloudflare
  static_configs:
    - targets: [exporter:8080]

- job_name: cloudflare-alt
  static_configs:
    - targets: [exporter:8080]


So exporter is scraped twice, 2x metrics in Prometheus.

_________________________________________________________________





metric_relabel_configs:
  - separator: ;
    regex: ^host$
    replacement: $1
    action: labeldrop

  - source_labels: [account]
    separator: ;
    regex: (.*)
    target_label: cf_account
    replacement: $1
    action: replace

  - source_labels: [zone]
    separator: ;
    regex: (.*)
    target_label: cf_zone
    replacement: $1
    action: replace



scrape_configs:
  - job_name: cloudflare-metrics
    scrape_interval: 30s
    static_configs:
      - targets: ['exporter:8080']
    metric_relabel_configs:




Factor	Internal	Customer
Exporter setup	| Single exporter	| Possibly running 2 exporters
Prometheus config	| Scraped once per 30s	| Scraped twice (by 2 jobs or clusters)
Zones monitored	| Maybe fewer zones	| More active zones
API query window	| Aligned	| Overlapping time windows
Grafana dashboard logic	| Rate per zone	| Maybe mis-aggregated



